summary:
- topic: Kaler Elementary Schedule
  text: The board unanimously approved a modified end-of-year schedule for Kaler Elementary
    to facilitate the school's closure and move. The new schedule includes an early
    release on June 15th and no school on June 16th.
- topic: Childcare for Kaler Families
  text: The district will provide free childcare through the rec program for Kaler
    families affected by the schedule change. The board discussed exploring additional
    creative solutions with community partners to cover any gaps in care.
- topic: Kaler Student Placement
  text: The administration reported on the ongoing waiver process for Kaler families
    seeking different school placements and noted that open houses at the receiving
    schools have been well-attended and positive.
- topic: Interim Superintendent
  text: The board approved a contract for Andy Wallace to serve as interim superintendent
    for two weeks in July. He will receive four vacation days as compensation instead
    of a salary.
- topic: Asst. Superintendent Recognition
  text: A unanimous vote approved a one-time $12,000 contribution to Assistant Superintendent
    Dr. Prince's retirement plan in recognition of her extensive work on the budget
    and staffing models, which went far beyond her normal duties.
- topic: Personnel Resignation
  text: The superintendent announced the resignation of Mike Nally, Director of Operations
    and Safety, effective August 1st. Board members praised his significant contributions
    to the district's safety and security.
- topic: Community Engagement
  text: The administration shared positive reports of PTA leaders and school communities
    actively planning events to welcome incoming Kaler families, fostering a sense
    of inclusion.
